{{also|Unto}}
==English==

===Etymology===
By analogy with {{term|until}}, substituting {{term|to}} for {{term|till}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-unto.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Conjunction===
{{en-con}}

# {{obsolete}} Up to the [[time]] or [[degree]] that; [[until]]; [[till]].

===Preposition===
{{en-preposition}}

# {{archaic|or|poetic}} Up to, indicating a motion towards a thing and then stopping at it.
#: ''Sir Gawain rode '''unto''' the nearby castle.''

=====Translations=====
{{trans-top|Up to}}
* French: {{t+|fr|jusqu'à}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Latin: {{t+|la|ad}}, {{t+|la|usque}}, {{t+|la|sub}}
{{trans-bottom}}

